0..68 Comment "// `then` and `cong` in a type take their types from their operands."
69..71 Comment "//"
72..145 Comment "// A path between paths states its endpoints with these forms, as a paper"
146..219 Comment "// writes them. A wrapper definition that only restates an operand\'s type"
220..244 Comment "// hides that statement."
245..247 Comment "//"
248..316 Comment "// Each declaration states a composite or an action in its own type."
317..319 Comment "//"
320..383 Comment "// - see: #3772 — `then` and `cong` in a type, refused before"
